// Merkle tree gadgets over the MiMC two-to-one compression. A node absorbs its left
// child through four rounds, folds in the right child, and absorbs four more, so
// `compress2` is the internal node these trees are built from. `merkle_step` climbs one
// level of an authentication path: it orders the running node and its sibling by the
// path bit, then compresses the ordered pair. Fold the step over a path of siblings to
// verify membership under a public root; the shield note tree and the merkle examples
// share this one construction. Path bits and any decomposed inputs must be constrained
// as bits by the caller.
include "hash.zkl";
include "logic.zkl";

// The first four rounds, from the first four round constants.
fn absorb_lo(s) = mimc_round(mimc_round(mimc_round(mimc_round(s, MIMC_C[0]), MIMC_C[1]), MIMC_C[2]), MIMC_C[3]);

// The next four rounds, from the following four constants.
fn absorb_hi(s) = mimc_round(mimc_round(mimc_round(mimc_round(s, MIMC_C[4]), MIMC_C[5]), MIMC_C[6]), MIMC_C[7]);

// Two-to-one compression: absorb the left child, fold in the right, absorb four more.
fn compress2(left, right) = absorb_hi(absorb_lo(left) + right);

// One level of an authentication path. The path bit b is one when the running node sits
// on the right, so the sibling becomes the left child; order the pair by b and compress.
fn merkle_step(node, sib, b) = compress2(mux(b, sib, node), mux(b, node, sib));
